From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sapi: voice properties, event source, status, outputs, Skip, SpeakStream, automation

sapi: voice properties, event source, status, outputs, Skip, SpeakStream, automation

The ISpVoice and ISpeechVoice stubs, all FIXME returning E_NOTIMPL, behave as
documented now. An engine is needed to speak, so what the audit lists as
"needs an engine" is driven through the engine site.

- New events.c: the event queue and notification of an event source:
  SetInterest (both masks need the SPFEI flag bits and the queued events
  are a part of the interest, E_INVALIDARG otherwise), GetEvents (events
  leave the queue, strings and objects are copied for the queue and owned by
  the caller afterwards), GetInfo, and the notifications: sink, window
  message, callback function, callback interface (a C++ class with one
  virtual method) and Win32 event (signaled while events are queued,
  WaitForNotifyEvent is S_OK or S_FALSE on time out and SPERR_UNINITIALIZED
  without one, a second notification is SPERR_ALREADY_INITIALIZED).
- ISpVoice: those event source members; priority and alert boundary (only
  TTS events) and sync speak timeout properties; GetStatus (stream numbers,
  last result, running state, the last word and sentence position,
  bookmark, phoneme and viseme, kept up to date from the events of the
  engine); SpeakCompleteEvent; GetOutputObjectToken (S_FALSE when the
  output is a stream) and GetOutputStream (both create the default output
  when there is none); Pause and Resume (the audio output is paused);
  Skip (asks the engine through its site: GetSkipInfo reports the sentences
  to skip, CompleteSkip answers); SpeakStream (text streams as ANSI, UTF-16
  or UTF-8 with a byte order mark, wave streams played to the output without
  an engine); Speak with SPF_IS_FILENAME; IsUISupported and DisplayUI
  through the engine and audio tokens.
- The engine site: AddEvents (stamps the stream number, feeds status and
  queue), GetEventInterest, GetSkipInfo, CompleteSkip, and ISpEventSink on
  QueryInterface. Every stream raises SPEI_START_INPUT_STREAM and
  SPEI_END_INPUT_STREAM around the engine.
- ISpeechVoice: Status (new ISpeechVoiceStatus object, a snapshot),
  AudioOutput and AudioOutputStream (any other output is presented as a
  file stream object), Rate, Priority, AlertBoundary, EventInterests,
  SynchronousSpeakTimeout, AllowAudioOutputFormatChangesOnNextSet,
  SpeakStream, Pause, Resume, Skip, GetAudioOutputs, WaitUntilDone,
  SpeakCompleteEvent, IsUISupported and DisplayUI.
- async_empty_queue reports how many tasks it dropped, so the voice knows
  how many speak tasks are still pending.

